00:07:20.656 --> 00:07:23.498
We are gonna finally get started on the roof.

00:07:27.315 --> 00:07:30.968
- Ok, so, the structure of the toilet has been completed.

00:07:30.968 --> 00:07:35.307
But, the roof has not been covered yet,
 and we need to do something...

00:07:35.307 --> 00:07:41.557
Because, all the small things and also the rain,
they would slip into the cracks.

00:07:41.557 --> 00:07:43.661
So, we need to cover the roof with something.

00:07:44.023 --> 00:07:46.487
We are always struggling to find roof options.

00:07:46.703 --> 00:07:50.854
Around here, you find corrugated sheets or ceramic roof tiles.

00:07:50.854 --> 00:07:51.952
But, that's kind of it!

00:07:51.952 --> 00:07:55.936
We'd like to try and find other options of reused materials.

00:07:56.144 --> 00:08:01.138
We already made one with recycled plastic that kind of does the job.

00:08:01.138 --> 00:08:04.412
And now, we will try an even more local method:

00:08:04.523 --> 00:08:09.372
Aluminum cans, that we have been collecting since the beginning of the season.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:13.406
So, the first step is to clean them.

00:08:16.272 --> 00:08:19.178
After that, take the top and bottom of the can off.

00:08:19.842 --> 00:08:24.325
For that I made a tool back in Hong Kong, that does the job way faster.

00:08:39.227 --> 00:08:42.390
And now, we just cut a straight line the can in the middle of the can.

00:08:45.599 --> 00:08:48.142
Now, you get a piece of sheet metal!

00:08:50.521 --> 00:08:57.189
So, when we go out to look for examples where people use
 aluminum cans to make the roof shingles...

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.170
There are different examples.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:08.089
The most simple way is that people 
putting it one over another and using a stapler.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:17.452
There are some problems, because when you staple it, 
you create holes where water could go in...

00:09:17.452 --> 00:09:20.164
Also, when there is wind it creates a lot of noise.

00:09:20.164 --> 00:09:27.673
The most stable example is when people fold it into this shape 
and click on to each other,

00:09:27.673 --> 00:09:30.206
That way, the water won't go in from the sides so easily.

00:09:30.206 --> 00:09:35.362
But still, from the top the water might 'sneak' through...

00:09:36.405 --> 00:09:45.148
So, that's why we come to this solution, 
to having each shingle folded on the side and also on the top.

00:09:45.535 --> 00:09:53.088
When we put it on to each other, they click on the sides
 and on the top, so the water won't go in so easily.

00:09:53.309 --> 00:10:01.857
And then, we used this little tap from the can to press it down
without putting any holes on the shingles.

00:10:01.857 --> 00:10:05.326
So, I think this will be the direction we are going to go in!

00:10:05.539 --> 00:10:11.000
So, to create a shingle from this, to this, it takes a few steps.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.480
The first step is to cut a shape.

00:10:36.128 --> 00:10:45.009
Since we have to create a few hundred of these shingles, 
and we have to make sure each one of them keeps the similar shape...

00:10:45.009 --> 00:10:46.568
We have to create a mold.

00:11:14.779 --> 00:11:15.779
There's one shingle!

00:11:16.636 --> 00:11:23.011
After measuring the size of the roof, 
I noticed that we needed more cans than we can collect in the Kamp.

00:11:23.236 --> 00:11:24.236
- What are you doing right now?

00:11:24.589 --> 00:11:28.696
I'm making a poster to get cans from the neighbors.

00:11:28.696 --> 00:11:34.319
So, I made a small poster and ask for the local cafés
 to collect the cans together with us.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.000
Just after some weeks:

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:43.166
We are going to pick up some cans from the neighbors.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:50.133
There is a really nice café here and the owner, 
Elisabeth, has been collecting cans for us!

00:11:50.133 --> 00:11:53.776
Let's go and see what's inside!

00:12:05.609 --> 00:12:07.609
So, here is our catch!

00:12:09.885 --> 00:12:11.084
This is unique one!

00:12:11.084 --> 00:12:11.885
We don't see it very often.

00:12:21.253 --> 00:12:22.253
Here are the cans.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.640
We already have enough cans for the roof.

00:12:34.226 --> 00:12:38.328
We noticed they come in these two sizes usually.

00:12:38.759 --> 00:12:43.331
To accommodate them in the design of the roof...

00:12:43.418 --> 00:12:53.960
We need to fold them in a way that different sizes of cans
can still interlock with each other, just like that.

00:12:54.262 --> 00:13:01.217
You can imagine that in a process 
we would create a lot of gaps in between.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:07.556
We made this kind of prototype 
and we're gonna put it under the shower.

00:13:07.833 --> 00:13:11.821
We'll see if the water actually come through from the back, so...

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.880
I think the results seem to be promising!

00:13:38.746 --> 00:13:46.195
OK, I think it's safe to say that the water 
doesn't go through for the small one.

00:13:46.824 --> 00:13:48.824
Let's go to the big one!

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:20.550
So, the corners have been trimmed.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:27.000
The next step is folding them halfway with 
the mold to mark the folding line.

00:14:29.748 --> 00:14:30.720
Here we go!

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:52.000
So, they have been folded halfway.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.009
But, there's still one more step...

00:14:55.009 --> 00:15:01.383
We need to fold it all the way back,
just so that they can interlock with each other.

00:15:01.621 --> 00:15:05.615
For this part, I think we gather everyone 
and ask for some help.

00:15:05.615 --> 00:15:06.600
Let's go!

00:15:56.604 --> 00:16:00.236
So, here is the roof of the new toilet.

00:16:00.653 --> 00:16:07.942
Before we install tiles, we need to put on 
these aluminum edges around the roof.

00:16:08.297 --> 00:16:13.169
It's kind of for the tiles to grab on to the roof.

00:16:14.769 --> 00:16:15.395
Let's do it!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.496
Yes, it's finished! It's done!

00:18:30.819 --> 00:18:32.730
- The first thing in the morning and I just woke up!

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:33.554
Amazing!

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:39.585
- You have to record your face Gui right now!

00:18:39.585 --> 00:18:41.046
Yeah! Turn the camera around!

00:18:43.797 --> 00:18:50.044
After so many people drinking, having so many days
 and so much effort: the roof is finally done!

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:02.141
- So, there's the roof!

00:19:02.141 --> 00:19:04.053
This is a completely new kind of roof design.

00:19:04.053 --> 00:19:07.366
An experiment to try and find more recycled materials to work with.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:13.493
If you want to download the drawings of the mold, 
in order to replicate it, or follow how it will behave over time...

00:19:13.493 --> 00:19:17.208
Click the link in the description below, 
so you can follow it in the research module!

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:22.391
Now, we need to wait until rain comes,
 see how it actually holds up and if you can poop dry.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:26.479
Sometimes things take time before
 you see if a creation works out.

00:19:26.479 --> 00:19:30.609
Just like a few years ago, we planted this young peach tree when we arrived here.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:34.000
- We planted it about 2 and a half to 3 years ago?

00:19:34.253 --> 00:19:39.560
We have our trees and bushes, so it's time to start planting.

00:19:42.192 --> 00:19:46.309
Last year, it had a few fruits, 
but this year was really, really heavy.

00:19:46.309 --> 00:19:49.712
It was even falling into the pathway that we have.

00:19:49.712 --> 00:19:55.280
About half of the fruits were already eaten by the people, 
and the rest is starting to be eaten by the ants.

00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:59.797
So, it's time to collect them all, 
and put them in a fresh place without the ants.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:28.894
- You can see the ants are just going into defensive mode.

00:20:28.894 --> 00:20:32.265
"Gather everything! It's your last chance!"

00:20:50.765 --> 00:20:54.000
- This is the greatest harvest of this tree.

00:20:54.792 --> 00:20:57.358
Still quite some juicy peaches to go...

00:21:04.598 --> 00:21:06.902
- Alright, so, that was it for this video!

00:21:08.597 --> 00:21:10.117
Thanks for watching!

00:21:10.484 --> 00:21:11.519
This is actually not a peach...

00:21:11.519 --> 00:21:15.444
It's a pear, because the peaches got eaten very fast, 
because they were delicious.

